e ownership.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm the endpoint-attribution seam is single-owner and consistent between T2 (fuse resolves via coordinator.locate(identity) on TicketOutcome) and the parent/T3 model (coordinator tags each outcome with (provider, endpoint)).","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7231,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent 'Attribution': 'OperationOutcome carries logical_id + authoritative failure_scope but no endpoint id, so the coordinator (the adapter's caller) tags each outcome with the (provider, endpoint) it dispatched to; inferred counters key off that identity.'","T2 'Attribution': 'coordinator.TicketOutcome carries identity, disposition, failure_scope but no endpoint id; the (provider, endpoint) identity for an outcome is resolved from the coordinator's locate(identity) binding mapping ... The fuse keys inferred counters off that resolved identity.'","T3 guard section names the signature coordinator.coordinate(ticket_plans, *, execute, locate, budget_factory), implying locate is supplied to the coordinator, aligning with T2's resolve-via-locate model rather than the parent's coordinator-tags model.","container pairing: parent + 67d4-ecba-cf95-4353/d0ec-da23-32ba-47c6/dd65-54fa-f4c3-4bc9"],"finding":"T2 and the parent/T3 assign the endpoint-attribution seam to DIFFERENT components: the parent (and T3's guard model) says the coordinator, as the adapter's caller, tags each outcome with the (provider, endpoint) it dispatched to; T2 instead says the fuse resolves the (provider, endpoint) identity itself from coordinator.locate(identity) on TicketOutcome. Verify these two ownership models are the same seam and not two competing implementations.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f98408e4b87c7d3c2","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"child dd65-54fa-f4c3-4bc9 (T2), 'Fuse scope, eligibility & counter semantics — Attribution'","norm_id":"nd217aa1c848d4ade","priority":0.2269,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An op on endpoint E1 exhausts its budget; the fuse must attribute the outcome to (provider, E1). If the coordinator is expected to have already stamped (provider, endpoint) on the outcome (parent/T3 tag model) but the fuse instead calls locate(identity) (T2 model), the endpoint id may be sourced twice or neither side owns it, mis-keying the per-endpoint counter.","Provider-scope threshold (>=2 distinct endpoints) depends on correct per-outcome endpoint identity; a seam mismatch could collapse two endpoints to one or split one into two."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Pick one owner for endpoint attribution and state it identically in the parent box, T2, and T3: e.g. the coordinator resolves (provider, endpoint) via the injected locate(identity) and stamps it on TicketOutcome, and the fuse consumes that stamped identity (never re-resolving), so all three describe the same seam.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"insufficient","impact_follows_necessarily":"insufficient","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"insufficient","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"insufficient"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile step 2's disposition names with the canonical OperationOutcome names used in the resolution section (map auto-healed→recovered, deferred→retryable_deferred, success→applied/already_satisfied) so one vocabulary is used throughout.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","F1","T2","T4"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8368,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 2: 'Normalize auto-healed, success, deferred, permanent, commit-unknown, exhausted transient, and skipped dispositions'","Resolution section uses: 'applied/recovered/already_satisfied', 'permanent_failure', 'exhausted_transient', terminal 'retryable_deferred'"],"finding":"Step 2's disposition names ('auto-healed, success, deferred, permanent, commit-unknown, exhausted transient, skipped') and the resolution section's names ('applied', 'recovered', 'already_satisfied', 'permanent_failure', 'commit_unknown', 'exhausted_transient', 'retryable_deferred') are near-synonyms with no explicit mapping, so a reader must infer that 'auto-healed'='recovered', 'deferred'='retryable_deferred', 'exhausted transient'='exhausted_transient'.","group_criter